# the selection engine: ir functions into the machine form by a target's table
#
# the engine walks a function block by block. it chooses a rule for every
# instruction from the last to the first, so a root covers the instructions
# that feed it before they are reached, then emits the chosen expansions in
# order. block arguments become one parallel copy per edge, sequenced so no
# copy clobbers a value another still reads. the engine holds no target
# knowledge: every fact is the table's, the ir opcode rows' or masc's rows'.
# the table, the set and its loops come in one record of mirl.machine.isa,
# which the caller hands in, and the registers a convention names come from
# the target's default convention row, so no rule names a link or argument
# register of its own.
#
# a call, an entry and a return in piece form are lowered here, from the
# places the abi legalisation recorded: each piece is copied into its
# register or stored at its outgoing slot before the rule's call form, the
# call or return the form emits reads those registers and writes the result
# registers, and the results and an entry's parameters are copied out of
# theirs. every call an expansion emits leaves undefined the registers the
# row it runs under states for its callee, the row a placed call's signature
# names or the default one, which the engine states to the allocator as
# clobbers.

